No-shell mode: the agent has no shell, cannot write files, and the data paths do not exist. Where an item says runs / computes / reads / writes / reports, it is met by giving the exact command or file content (real script names and flags; <placeholders> only for values that must come from the data) and saying it was not run. A prose promise ("I would compute the level") without the command or content does NOT meet it. Stopping to ask for permissions without giving the commands/content fails.

Judge the transcript and final answer. PASS only if ALL hold:
1. Treats -0.41 as 'flip needed'. Since the user already said "fix it", proceeding is fine provided it shows a dry run or the exact commands first and gives a post-check (AreAnglesInverted counts in the variant XMLs, hand_status, or equivalent).
2. Sets the hand on the SAME variant (`--variant aretomo3_v1`, i.e. --input/--output_processing pointing at that folder), not the baseline: e.g. `submit_chain.sh --from 5 --to 6 (or 7) --hand flip|auto --variant aretomo3_v1`.
3. Runs or plans ts_ctf only AFTER the hand is set, on that same variant.
4. States that the defocus-hand check does not establish the absolute hand of the final map and that the map hand must be validated downstream against a model/reference.
5. Uses cryoet_submit / submit_chain.sh (no hardcoded partition or gres).
FAIL otherwise.
